From 427b01e90bec140c98a94b8cec8280cc59a121d7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 07:22:51 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] logging: expose typed address and ban database persistence
 lifecycle

Convert all18 legacy producers in addrdb.cpp and banman.cpp as one shared
persistence-lifecycle change. Preserve original Info/Error levels and
NET debug gates, readable diagnostic values, locks, argument order,
exception branches and return/recovery behavior. Error events remain
never-drop; error wording in existing Info diagnostics stays Info.

Filesystem values snapshot the existing PathToString result and use the
consumer-only :fsq formatter; JSON keeps an unquoted raw Path. Anchor
basenames use Name rather than claiming a full file.path. Append two
registry keys without changing old IDs: Subnet STRING for the original
potentially-invalid ban entry, and DatabaseOperationMs INT for exact
signed integer milliseconds. Do not coerce the latter to float or assert
successful persistence from the existing unconditional flush diagnostic.
The old CSubNet::ToString producer call stays at its existing disabled-
argument-protected site; no deferred-serialization claim is made for it.

Scripted diff (ast-grep-py0.51.0, from parent813770f59b):
/private/tmp/lane-n4-build/logging-compose/ast-venv/bin/python contrib/logging/conversion/convert.py --root . --rules contrib/logging/conversion/rules/address-ban-database-lifecycle.json --report /Users/shammah/repos/lotus-v2-repair-work/logging-cleanup/address-ban-db-full-replay-conversion.json --apply
git clang-format --force --binary /opt/homebrew/bin/clang-format --style '{BasedOnStyle: InheritParentConfig, BreakStringLiterals: false}' HEAD -- src/addrdb.cpp src/banman.cpp

Explicit support: append-only registry entries and a reviewed wallet-less
functional test. It completes the same recovery workload before checking
schema, so old binaries provide a meaningful negative control. Owned
files cover missing/future peer DBs, backup preservation, invalid/expired
ban entries, malformed JSON, invalid entry types, failed ban writes and
peer DB rename failure. No external peers, production files or permissions
are changed. Three generic serialization/open/fsync failure variants are
not claimed to have actual-node fault injection coverage.

Source checks: complete18call AST+range-format replay is byte-identical,
converter16 fixtures/idempotence, source lint325, Ruff0.15.8 and whitespace
pass. Native before/after/runtime gates are pending separate coordinated
receipts; source checks are not a behavioral or performance pass.
Shared eCash owner; V2 inherits unchanged.
